{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261108T153705Z-7a103cdc", "ts": "2026-11-08T15:39:50Z", "actor": {"worktree": "arrt", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "release/v0.8.0", "build": "39144ab1f1d5"}, "body": {"base_commit": "f3ccae0c2d6ddff39b9f85b73235ada8175e45ed", "base_tree": "96e39076a8faf9f73c8b7f5e19c0b5fa75c2dd74", "head_tree": "6e7ab5c28fd51f9eb0b3c74dab30e57edbf96431", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "f3ccae0c2d6ddff39b9f85b73235ada8175e45ed", "mode": "final (full review, ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "rule-3 final: no build plan, session diff has 12 changed files (medium+ work \u2014 full review warranted)", "stage": "inner", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".github/workflows/api-drift.yml", ".github/workflows/browser.yml", ".github/workflows/suites.yml", ".python-version", "arrt/.python-version", "arrt/Dockerfile", "arrt/pyproject.toml", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/migrations.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_wall_migration.py", "contract/pyproject.toml", "pyproject.toml", "tests/test_one_python.py"], "files_changed": [".github/workflows/api-drift.yml", ".github/workflows/browser.yml", ".github/workflows/suites.yml", ".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v0.8.0.md", ".prawduct/change-log.md", ".python-version", "arrt/.python-version", "arrt/Dockerfile", "arrt/pyproject.toml", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/migrations.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_wall_migration.py", "contract/pyproject.toml", "pyproject.toml", "tests/test_one_python.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v0.8.0.md", ".prawduct/change-log.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: read core.md and tooling.md; one amended-wording survivor, nothing escalates", "recommendation": "Scope: none for the cross-check itself. The rule that applies is 'When you retire, amend, descope or close anything, first grep the whole repo (no --include) for its nouns and OLD wording'. The Dockerfile's `uv python install 3.14` is gone, but the same command survives as the stated method in .prawduct/artifacts/operational-spec.md section 'The Curation Interpreter' (line 152) and in the project-state.yaml decision at line 1977. Both describe the older Pi deployment, so nobody is led into a wrong action and nothing escalates. The other rules checked held: 'Stage new files before recording suite evidence' (.python-version and tests/test_one_python.py are both staged as A); 'When a check can be quiet for more than one reason' (test_every_ci_job_runs_the_uv_the_image_runs asserts that it found at least one setup-uv step); 'When a test, lint or check is new or rewritten, watch it fail once' (the change-log records 4 of 5 failing against the old tree and the fifth broken on purpose). No learnings rule was added or changed in this cycle.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile", "tests/test_one_python.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog reconciliation: no open item is resolved by this change", "recommendation": "Scope: none. `cache-query affecting` over the 14 changed files returned 0 items (cache confirmed 2026-11-08T15:05Z). A scan of the 19 open items for python/sqlite/uv/CI/docker/migration turned up only #263 (git ls-files guards skip untracked files). This change does not resolve it, and its new files are staged. C-B1 to C-B4: nothing to report, because no item was created or cited.", "files": [".prawduct/change-log.md"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: covered release-plan-v0.8.0.md and change-log.md (the one-python entry, seven release=v0.8.0 tags); nothing clears a bar", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The plan's '7 entries in 7 scopes' matches the seven release=v0.8.0 tags. The four no-plan scopes are named consistently. The claim that the contract version is unchanged holds, since contract/pyproject.toml gained only a [tool.uv] table. The change-log's 'holds all four copies in step' is followed by a list of five items. That is an imprecise count that nothing reads, so no edit is wanted. The Rollback section does not mention the raised SQLite floor, but rolling back restores v0.7.0's own floor and image, so following it leads to no wrong action.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v0.8.0.md", ".prawduct/change-log.md"], "fid": "R-3"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 3}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The operator note's 'rebuilt by the next uv sync' is unverified for the Mac's case, where Homebrew's 3.14.6 satisfies the exact pin", "recommendation": "The change-log says local virtualenvs built on a system or Homebrew Python get rebuilt by the next `uv sync`. On the Mac the existing .venv runs Homebrew 3.14.6, which matches the new 3.14.6 pin exactly. So the rebuild only happens if uv's environment check also rejects an unmanaged interpreter under `python-preference = \"only-managed\"`, and nothing recorded shows that it does. Either run `uv sync` once in arrt/ on the Mac and confirm `sys.base_prefix` and `sqlite3.sqlite_version` (3.53.1) afterwards, or change the note to say to delete .venv first. Per the core rule 'When you record something as verified, name what was measured', the claim needs a measurement or a hedge.", "files": ["arrt/pyproject.toml", "pyproject.toml", "contract/pyproject.toml"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "test_every_ci_job_runs_the_uv_the_image_runs only scans *.yml workflows", "recommendation": "`WORKFLOWS.glob(\"*.yml\")` skips any `*.yaml` workflow. There are none today, but GitHub runs both extensions, so a new `.yaml` workflow with an unpinned setup-uv would pass in silence. Glob both, or use `.github/workflows/*.y*ml` (core rule: 'When a safety check guards a filtered feature, range it over the population the hazard lives in').", "files": ["tests/test_one_python.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "The CPython patch procedure in two artifacts no longer describes how the interpreter changes", "recommendation": "Instance. After this change the image installs exactly what `.python-version` says (3.14.6), and only a uv that agrees with the image and CI. Rebuilding the image therefore never picks up a newer CPython. Patching means bumping the root pin and its `arrt/` copy, and the Dockerfile's uv tag plus every `setup-uv` version if the new patch needs a newer uv. `security-model.md` \u00a7 Supply Chain (Direction note: 'Patching it therefore means rebuilding and redeploying the image') and `operational-spec.md` \u00a7 Routine Operations ('Patch curation's CPython | `uv python upgrade 3.14`') still describe the old path. An operator acting on a CPython CVE rebuilds, gets 3.14.6 back and believes the patch is done. Make both point to `.python-version` and `tests/test_one_python.py` rather than restating the steps. The same section's 'no pinning or provenance policy has been decided' is also now partly overtaken.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile", ".python-version", ".prawduct/artifacts/security-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/operational-spec.md"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The uv version is written in nine places and a test keeps them equal, while a contributor's own uv is not pinned at all", "recommendation": "Class: any future uv bump edits the Dockerfile tag and eight `setup-uv` `version:` lines in lock step, and `test_every_ci_job_runs_the_uv_the_image_runs` catches only a missed one. Local `uv sync`, the 'Mac ran Homebrew' case the change-log names, is still uncovered. A single `[tool.uv] required-version` (root pyproject or a `uv.toml`) is one owner: uv enforces it locally, and setup-uv can read it, which would let the eight `version:` lines go. The test would then compare the Dockerfile against that one value. I did not check whether setup-uv@v5 auto-reads `required-version`; confirm that before dropping the explicit inputs. If the pin stays where it is, no edit is needed.", "files": [".github/workflows/suites.yml", ".github/workflows/browser.yml", ".github/workflows/api-drift.yml", "tests/test_one_python.py", "arrt/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Three pyproject.toml files carry the same five-line rationale that test_one_python.py's docstring already holds", "recommendation": "Instance, prose: no edit is required. It cites the learnings rule 'When a claim already lives in prose, verify it against the code and add a pointer, never a copy'. Each `[tool.uv]` comment repeats the incident story ('one suite read two SQLites the day CI's runner image changed (2026-11-08)') and also points to `tests/test_one_python.py`. The pointer alone does the work, so if the comments are ever touched, reduce each to that pointer.", "files": ["pyproject.toml", "arrt/pyproject.toml", "contract/pyproject.toml"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The setup-uv guard scans only *.yml, so a .yaml workflow would go unchecked without any notice", "recommendation": "Instance, cheap. It cites the learnings rule 'When you fix a defect, make inputs the fix does not know fail by name'. `WORKFLOWS.glob(\"*.yml\")` misses a `.yaml` workflow (GitHub accepts both) and any composite action under `.github/actions/`. A setup-uv step there would run an unpinned uv while the guard stays green. Glob both extensions, or assert that no `.yaml` file exists.", "files": ["tests/test_one_python.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "The docstring's reason for pinning uv may not be the mechanism once the Python pin is exact", "recommendation": "Prose, NOTE-weight. This is inference, not measurement. With `.python-version` at 3.14.6, a newer uv cannot pick a newer patch, which is the docstring's stated reason ('a newer uv knows newer patch releases'). What a newer uv plausibly can do is fetch a different python-build-standalone build of the same 3.14.6, with a different bundled SQLite, and that is the hazard this change exists to stop. If the guard is edited, state the reason it actually defends. Otherwise no edit is needed.", "files": ["tests/test_one_python.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "The toolchain policy (exact patch pin, only-managed, pinned uv) has its why only in the change-log and a test docstring, not in the artifact that owns the version", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. project-preferences.md section 'Language & Runtime' calls itself the canonical home for the curation plane's Python, and it still reads plain '3.14' with no mention of the exact pin or of the rule that only a uv-managed Python is used. A maintainer who reads it (as the other artifacts tell them to) and loosens .python-version to '3.14' would be stopped by the test, but would not learn why. Add a pointer there to tests/test_one_python.py, the one place that holds the rule, rather than a copy. When the next record amends this, also declare `Retires: uv python install 3.14`, so that record_lint's retired-claim-survives catches the operational-spec.md and project-state.yaml survivors.", "files": [".python-version", "arrt/pyproject.toml", "tests/test_one_python.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "The floor's comment says the guard exists so the failure names the remedy, but the refusal names only the version", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The comment on _DROP_COLUMN_SINCE says that below the floor the drop 'fails naming neither the version nor the remedy'. That implies _require_drop_column's RuntimeError names a remedy, but it states only the required and actual SQLite versions. Now that the remedy is concrete (run under the repository's pinned uv-managed Python, i.e. `uv sync` with python-preference only-managed), say so in the message, or drop 'nor the remedy' from the comment. Low cost. It matters only on the machine the comment calls 'the machine nobody is at'.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/persistence/migrations.py"], "oid": "O-9"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `release/v0.8.0`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/release-plan-v0.8.0.md", ".prawduct/change-log.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-08T15:37:06Z"}}

